<title>ABU DHABI: UAE to donate $2 million in food to Palestinians.</title>
<headline>UAE to donate $2 million in food to Palestinians.</headline>
<dateline>ABU DHABI 1997-03-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>United Arab Emirates President Sheikh Zaid bin Sultan al-Nahayan on Monday ordered the Abu Dhabi government to purchase $2 million in food supplies for Palestinians in the West Bank and Gaza Strip.</p>
<p>The official WAM news agency said the UAE Red Crescent Society would be in charge of organising the purchases.</p>
<p>The Gulf Arab state has often donated money to Palestinians.</p>
</text>
